{"name":"Ruby Ring","hex":"#a03d41","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ruby","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A clear, deep, red variety of corundum, valued as a precious stone.","A deep red colour."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a deep, red color; ruby-red."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ruby"},{"term":"ring","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A solid object in the shape of a circle.\nA circumscribing object, (roughly) circular and hollow, looking like an annual ring, earring, finger ring etc.","A circumscribing object, (roughly) circular and hollow, looking like an annual ring, earring, finger ring etc."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To enclose or surround.","To make an incision around; to girdle; to cut away a circular tract of bark from a tree in order to kill it."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ring"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ruby Ring","blocks":[{"text":"Ruby Ring is a 2013 South Korean television daily drama series starring Lee So-yeon, Im Jung-eun, Kim Suk-hoon and Park Gwang-hyun. It airs on KBS2 on Mondays to Fridays at 19:45 for 93 episodes beginning August 19, 2013."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c7/Ruby_Ring_%28%EB%A3%A8%EB%B9%84_%EB%B0%98%EC%A7%80%29_-_Promotional_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ruby_Ring"},{"title":"Ring (jewellery)","blocks":[{"text":"A ring is a round band, usually made of metal, worn as ornamental jewelry. The term \"ring\" by itself denotes jewellery worn on the finger; when worn as an ornament elsewhere, the body part is specified within the term, e.g., earrings, neck rings, arm rings, and toe rings. Rings fit snugly around or in the part of the body they ornament, so bands worn loosely, like a bracelet, are not rings. Rings may be made of almost any hard material: wood, bone, stone, metal, glass, jade, gemstone or plastic. They may be set with gemstones or with other types of stone or glass."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Ring_Ruby.jpg/330px-Ring_Ruby.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ring_(jewellery)"},{"title":"Ruby","blocks":[{"text":"Ruby is a pinkish-red to blood-red-colored gemstone, a variety of the mineral corundum, consisting of aluminium oxide (α-Al2O3). Ruby is one of the most popular traditional jewelry gems and is very durable. Other varieties of gem-quality corundum are called sapphires, and rubies are also sometimes referred to as \"red sapphires\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Corundum-215330.jpg/330px-Corundum-215330.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ruby"},{"title":"Ruby (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Ruby is a color that is a representation of the color of the cut and polished ruby gemstone and is a shade of red or pink."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Ruby_gem.JPG/330px-Ruby_gem.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ruby_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Ring_anatomy.png/330px-Ring_anatomy.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Ring_anatomy.png/330px-Ring_anatomy.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Anatomy of a solitary ring","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARing_anatomy.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Rings_from_the_snettisham_jewellers_hoard.JPG/500px-Rings_from_the_snettisham_jewellers_hoard.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https